WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:06.243
Hey! Welcome to a new Project Kamp update!

00:00:06.243 --> 00:00:10.231
Today, we have a special update, 
because we're gonna record&nbsp;it in one shot!

00:00:10.231 --> 00:00:11.701
It's super hot!

00:00:11.701 --> 00:00:15.360
We're gonna walk around, show you all the people,&nbsp;
and all the things we've been working on.

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:23.191
But, it might go wrong, because again it's super hot,
and the camera is probably gonna overheat?

00:00:23.191 --> 00:00:23.691
I'm not sure.

00:00:23.691 --> 00:00:24.962
I have a backup camera here.

00:00:24.962 --> 00:00:28.072
People might&nbsp;do stuff we don't want them to do...

00:00:28.072 --> 00:00:29.344
So, let's see!

00:00:29.344 --> 00:00:31.428
I got my spoon microphone right here.

00:00:31.870 --> 00:00:34.030
So, yeah, let's move around.

00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:35.260
We're starting in Basekamp!

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:37.307
Right here in the kitchen.

00:00:37.307 --> 00:00:43.860
And, just to show you that it's really hot, 
on the thermometer it's above 40 degrees (=104°F)!

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:50.038
Probably, it's maybe a few degrees hotter here,
 because&nbsp;we have the plastic roof.

00:00:50.038 --> 00:00:51.709
As you might have seen in the videos.

00:00:51.709 --> 00:00:55.578
It's really good to choose a&nbsp;black roof in a hot area...

00:00:55.873 --> 00:00:58.135
Makes it really fresh.

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:03.144
So, here we have the kitchen, 
where we have Dorian -- our new&nbsp;chef!

00:01:03.144 --> 00:01:04.227
- Hey!

00:01:04.227 --> 00:01:05.693
What are you cooking today?

00:01:05.693 --> 00:01:10.766
- We're making some mushroom goulash,
 and some mashed potatoes.

00:01:10.766 --> 00:01:13.500
We're gonna fry these aubergines as well!

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:15.363
- All right!

00:01:15.363 --> 00:01:16.370
Now, how is it to cook in here?

00:01:16.370 --> 00:01:17.354
Is it not too&nbsp;hot today?

00:01:17.354 --> 00:01:21.306
- It is very hot, and we also have to keep one of the doors closed.

00:01:21.306 --> 00:01:25.421
Because, the sun is shining on a really bad angle.

00:01:25.421 --> 00:01:27.704
So, yeah, it gets quite hot in here...

00:01:27.704 --> 00:01:29.459
- It sounds&nbsp;great to cook here...

00:01:29.459 --> 00:01:30.985
Okay, we'll continue! Thanks!

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:37.981
So, next, we'll go to the pizza hut, 
where&nbsp;Kevin is baking some bread.

00:01:37.981 --> 00:01:40.420
Which we do twice a week!

00:01:41.216 --> 00:01:44.366
We also bake pizza, but we also&nbsp;make bread.

00:01:44.602 --> 00:01:45.829
Look at them!

00:01:45.829 --> 00:01:46.706
Some of them are already done!

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:50.235
How's it going here, Kevin?

00:01:50.235 --> 00:01:52.635
- I'm making bread for&nbsp;everyone!

00:01:53.048 --> 00:01:54.871
Isn't it a bit hot to bake bread now?

00:01:54.871 --> 00:01:57.323
- Yes, but everyone needs to eat!

00:01:57.323 --> 00:01:58.701
That's true, that's true.

00:01:58.701 --> 00:02:01.613
How do you make sure stuff doesn't get on fire?

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:04.989
- Well, we spread water around the pizza&nbsp;oven.

00:02:04.989 --> 00:02:06.900
So, we make sure everything is moist.

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:09.866
- Cool! Sounds great!

00:02:09.866 --> 00:02:11.630
All right!

00:02:12.691 --> 00:02:14.601
Do you have&nbsp;anything to say to your friends in Hong Kong?

00:02:14.601 --> 00:02:17.826
- I'm coming back to&nbsp;make some peso de nada!

00:02:18.798 --> 00:02:20.417
All right!

00:02:21.770 --> 00:02:27.031
Let's continue here to show the&nbsp;area where we live.

00:02:27.031 --> 00:02:29.642
So, here are all the vans and the tents.

00:02:30.408 --> 00:02:32.757
This is the yellow van that we recently renovated.

00:02:32.757 --> 00:02:33.660
Go see it in the update!

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:35.659
Alice is working here.

00:02:35.659 --> 00:02:39.420
Oh! I think she's in a call or something, so we just let her work.

00:02:42.651 --> 00:02:45.398
Let's go down there.

00:02:45.398 --> 00:02:50.685
Here, we&nbsp;also have a nice place to chill, 
which has a lot of hammocks.

00:02:50.685 --> 00:02:54.436
So, when it's hot, it's a good&nbsp;place to take a siesta.

00:02:54.996 --> 00:02:56.780
Here we have Rita!

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:58.686
What are you doing here, Rita?

00:02:58.686 --> 00:03:01.980
- Well,&nbsp;we're taking care of the baby!

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:04.257
Is it nice to have a baby here?

00:03:04.257 --> 00:03:05.923
- It's really cool!

00:03:05.923 --> 00:03:09.964
We all do some shifts of taking care of the baby.

00:03:09.964 --> 00:03:12.512
Just so that the baby has a bit more diversity.

00:03:12.512 --> 00:03:14.520
It's enjoying the microphone a lot right now!

00:03:16.672 --> 00:03:18.444
- The baby doesn't say much, huh?

00:03:18.444 --> 00:03:23.627
And then, the parents can&nbsp;also have a bit of free time
 doing other things besides parenting.

00:03:23.627 --> 00:03:25.278
It works really nice!

00:03:25.278 --> 00:03:26.713
- So, is&nbsp;this your baby?

00:03:26.713 --> 00:03:28.304
Not my baby.

00:03:28.746 --> 00:03:30.706
- A community baby!

00:03:35.171 --> 00:03:37.939
We will continue down here.

00:03:38.794 --> 00:03:42.495
Let's go to our latest and newest toilet.

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:45.917
Which we built right here!

00:03:45.917 --> 00:03:50.945
So, that's the old&nbsp;toilet we used to have,
 and we recently made an upgrade to this toilet.

00:03:50.945 --> 00:03:54.803
It has a bunch of upgrades, and Alejandro is right here!

00:03:54.803 --> 00:03:57.522
What are you doing here, Alejandro?

00:03:58.819 --> 00:04:02.436
- The poop bucket is pretty full,
 so we have to&nbsp;put in a new one.

00:04:02.672 --> 00:04:04.059
You need a hand, I see..

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:09.608
So, how often do you do this?

00:04:09.608 --> 00:04:15.005
- Every day, when the&nbsp;bucket is full,
 we have to put it there in the bucket station and put a new one.

00:04:15.005 --> 00:04:17.185
So, we can fill it again&nbsp;tomorrow!

00:04:17.185 --> 00:04:22.345
- Okay, so, this is the sewage system of Project Kamp?

00:04:22.345 --> 00:04:26.576
Yeah, this is our lovely sewage system, 
&nbsp;with our bucket station for the buckets!

00:04:26.576 --> 00:04:31.054
We put them here and cover them with a lovely lid.

00:04:31.054 --> 00:04:35.100
And then, after a week, we put them here in the Poop Palace.

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:37.511
- What is this?

00:04:37.511 --> 00:04:40.603
This is the Poop Palace, where we keep all of the compost.

00:04:40.603 --> 00:04:43.779
You can see already we have two full ones after a month.

00:04:43.779 --> 00:04:45.780
So, we are using it a lot!

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:48.055
- Who's living in the Palace?

00:04:48.055 --> 00:04:51.051
So far, no&nbsp;one, but it's always open, if you want to join!

00:04:51.051 --> 00:04:53.253
- It's still available people!

00:04:53.253 --> 00:04:54.360
All right, thanks!

00:04:56.880 --> 00:05:00.546
So, we can go here to our unofficial route.

00:05:00.546 --> 00:05:05.870
We&nbsp;kind of have to go here now
 to make one nice shot and one nice walk.

00:05:05.870 --> 00:05:07.689
But otherwise, we would&nbsp;have walked back.

00:05:07.689 --> 00:05:08.760
So: this is for you, YouTube!

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:12.754
This area is actually what we've&nbsp;recently debarked

00:05:13.196 --> 00:05:18.086
So, from all the trees here, we took off the bark from the bottom.

00:05:18.086 --> 00:05:20.916
They&nbsp;would die in a few years, and don't re-sprout.

00:05:20.916 --> 00:05:26.782
But, recently, a lot of resin started to come out, which is kind of cool.

00:05:26.782 --> 00:05:27.877
We don't know what to do with it!

00:05:27.877 --> 00:05:30.960
It doesn't really smell very&nbsp;nice.

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:31.596
Well, not bad either...

00:05:31.596 --> 00:05:32.873
It just doesn't really smell.

00:05:33.757 --> 00:05:35.684
But, it feels like quite a cool material!

00:05:35.684 --> 00:05:39.631
It's really that every tree around here is now just losing resin!

00:05:39.631 --> 00:05:41.957
So, it would be cool to figure out&nbsp;what to do with that.

00:05:42.429 --> 00:05:45.698
But, yeah, the main principle is that we want 
to get rid of the mimosa trees here.

00:05:45.698 --> 00:05:48.060
This is an approach that would take a few years.

00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:52.902
But ideally, they're then really gone and don't re-sprout

00:05:55.407 --> 00:05:57.435
This is actually where we kind of do it for!

00:05:57.435 --> 00:06:01.295
These little oak trees -- the&nbsp;native trees from around here.

00:06:01.295 --> 00:06:02.931
We hope that they will grow.

00:06:02.931 --> 00:06:05.760
But, currently, it's very hard for&nbsp;them,
because the mimosas just take all the sun...

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:12.420
So, we cherish them, and hopefully one day,
these guys are the biggest trees here!

00:06:13.576 --> 00:06:15.480
But, it's gonna take few years...

00:06:18.794 --> 00:06:20.940
Here, we tried something else to get rid of them.

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:24.867
So, just to address the YouTube comments you&nbsp;guys all had:

00:06:24.867 --> 00:06:27.120
''Why do you leave stumps this long?''

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:29.974
The main reason is that they just sprout back

00:06:29.974 --> 00:06:35.964
In this way, it would be easier to maintain,
 because we can take off all the things that pop&nbsp;off.

00:06:35.964 --> 00:06:37.785
So, it doesn't become a big new tree again.

00:06:37.785 --> 00:06:41.055
But, we're not sure it's very effective...

00:06:41.055 --> 00:06:44.085
Maybe, chopping&nbsp;it down on the bottom is easier,
because then you can brush cut it.

00:06:44.085 --> 00:06:48.511
It's an experiment, but we either&nbsp;way would
 take care of this later in the year.

00:06:48.511 --> 00:06:49.530
We still want to do it!

00:06:49.530 --> 00:06:52.628
We'd plant a few more&nbsp;fruit trees,
 but you can see more of that later!

00:06:52.628 --> 00:06:55.606
Well, I hope, because that means we've done it.

00:06:56.991 --> 00:07:00.657
All right, so, let's have a look in our office!

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:04.193
In our beautiful ruin, with Portuguese&nbsp;quality.

00:07:04.193 --> 00:07:07.140
A solid build! 

00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:12.154
So, here we are in the office.

00:07:13.451 --> 00:07:17.481
I'm usually not allowed&nbsp;to have shoes in here,
 but I'll just do it for you guys, so it's faster.

00:07:17.481 --> 00:07:21.526
So here we usually have the video&nbsp;editors.

00:07:21.526 --> 00:07:22.151
This is Tincho!

00:07:22.151 --> 00:07:27.944
Usually, we would have Guillerme as well, 
but he's currently on holiday...

00:07:27.944 --> 00:07:30.035
He's with us always in the background.

00:07:30.035 --> 00:07:31.187
Isn't he, Tincho?

00:07:31.187 --> 00:07:32.536
- He's always with us!

00:07:33.125 --> 00:07:34.320
How is it going here?

00:07:34.674 --> 00:07:35.748
- Very good!

00:07:35.748 --> 00:07:38.200
I'm working on the next update about the can roof.

00:07:38.200 --> 00:07:39.562
So, yeah, it's going well.

00:07:40.442 --> 00:07:41.237
- A good video?

00:07:41.532 --> 00:07:43.333
It will&nbsp;be a good one, yeah!

00:07:43.333 --> 00:07:45.340
- How is it working in the heat here?

00:07:45.340 --> 00:07:47.873
Kind of difficult sometimes!

00:07:47.873 --> 00:07:49.157
The&nbsp;computer doesn't work...

00:07:49.687 --> 00:07:52.322
There is too much heat, but we can manage it. With the mate, always...

00:07:52.322 --> 00:07:56.606
- They're used to&nbsp;the heat now!

00:07:56.606 --> 00:07:57.645
All right, thanks!

00:07:58.146 --> 00:08:00.584
Here, we have the other Guilherme.

00:08:02.087 --> 00:08:02.819
What are you doing?

00:08:02.819 --> 00:08:05.564
- I'm working on the Community Platform.

00:08:05.564 --> 00:08:07.239
What is the Community Platform?

00:08:07.239 --> 00:08:15.916
- So, it's a place where the online community&nbsp;can 
share knowledge, how-to's and resources.

00:08:16.020 --> 00:08:21.481
So, your coding software to make sure the&nbsp;
community can collaborate online?

00:08:21.481 --> 00:08:22.320
- Yeah, exactly.

00:08:23.400 --> 00:08:28.657
Yeah, I'm currently working on adding replies&nbsp;
to the research modules.

00:08:28.657 --> 00:08:31.570
So, you guys can reply and talk to each other.

00:08:32.425 --> 00:08:33.982
- Is it complex?

00:08:33.982 --> 00:08:36.495
No, but it&nbsp;requires a lot of work.

00:08:36.495 --> 00:08:43.412
So, if you guys have skills and want to help out,
 see the link in the description below!

00:08:44.060 --> 00:08:46.884
Let us know that you want to help.

00:08:46.884 --> 00:08:50.418
- Software developers: we can use your help!

00:08:50.418 --> 00:08:52.759
Also,&nbsp;online and remote, you can always help out!

00:08:53.496 --> 00:08:53.996
Thanks!

00:08:56.100 --> 00:09:01.860
All right, so, now we go down here,
 where the&nbsp;General Help team is working.

00:09:01.860 --> 00:09:09.390
They are chopping a lot of mimosas.

00:09:09.390 --> 00:09:14.400
The main reason for that is&nbsp;that it's 
currently very hot, so the fire season is starting.

00:09:15.180 --> 00:09:19.978
The neighbors have been telling us a lot&nbsp;
to chop the mimosas, but it's a lot.

00:09:19.978 --> 00:09:26.460
But, the main important one is the road,
 because it's also&nbsp;our escape from the place if it catches on fire.

00:09:27.360 --> 00:09:28.451
How's it going here?

00:09:28.451 --> 00:09:30.010
- Good and hot!

00:09:30.364 --> 00:09:34.436
We're making a cleared route,
 so we can easily escape when it's needed.

00:09:34.436 --> 00:09:36.619
- An emergency exit?

00:09:36.619 --> 00:09:38.861
Emergency exit is what we call it.

00:09:38.861 --> 00:09:39.691
- What do you have there?

00:09:39.691 --> 00:09:44.029
Firewood, that we are stacking up in a pile,
 so we can use&nbsp;it for winter!

00:09:44.029 --> 00:09:47.150
- Do you still like chopping the mimosas?

00:09:47.150 --> 00:09:50.182
Yes, but I'm speaking for myself!

00:09:50.182 --> 00:09:51.331
I&nbsp;still like the chopping of the mimosas!

00:09:51.331 --> 00:09:54.036
Everyone seems very happy there, so it's great!

00:09:54.419 --> 00:09:56.208
- It's almost finishing time too...

00:09:56.208 --> 00:09:56.963
All right! Cool!

00:09:57.900 --> 00:09:58.985
Yeah, it's a big job.

00:10:00.646 --> 00:10:01.836
All right!&nbsp;Good luck!

00:10:01.836 --> 00:10:02.712
- Thank you! Ciao!

00:10:02.712 --> 00:10:03.491
Ciao!

00:10:09.600 --> 00:10:13.320
So, yeah, as you can see,
they've been&nbsp;chopping all of this here.

00:10:13.320 --> 00:10:14.958
This also used to be mimosas.

00:10:15.341 --> 00:10:18.268
It's quite nice that it opens up&nbsp;the land much more!

00:10:19.476 --> 00:10:24.003
It would help in case of a fire,
 that we can go out more&nbsp;safe faster.

00:10:24.828 --> 00:10:28.545
So, here we have the Community Center!

00:10:29.507 --> 00:10:30.656
I'm guessing you've seen it before.

00:10:30.656 --> 00:10:31.887
It's this big ruin.

00:10:33.181 --> 00:10:35.580
Sadly, I don't really have a good update on this...

00:10:36.480 --> 00:10:40.120
We cleaned it a while ago.

00:10:40.120 --> 00:10:41.646
But, stuff is&nbsp;growing back.

00:10:43.058 --> 00:10:44.219
We need to clean it again...

00:10:44.219 --> 00:10:49.221
But, the main thing is that we're still in the process&nbsp;
of legalization and paperwork.

00:10:49.221 --> 00:10:52.255
We're making sure we have a good drawing,
 but it's a complex building...

00:10:52.255 --> 00:10:56.998
It&nbsp;has a lot of infrastructure,
 like sewage systems, electricity systems, water systems...

00:10:56.998 --> 00:10:58.592
So, it's going&nbsp;slow.

00:10:59.800 --> 00:11:01.140
I think I hear a car coming!

00:11:05.633 --> 00:11:08.280
I'm gonna try to wait for this&nbsp;one,
 because then I don't have to walk up.

00:11:08.940 --> 00:11:13.370
I think it's Timo that has come back
 from, usually, some shopping.

00:11:13.370 --> 00:11:14.700
So, maybe we can hop in the back?

00:11:19.380 --> 00:11:20.977
Hey Timo! How's it going?

00:11:20.977 --> 00:11:22.207
- Hi! It's going nice!

00:11:22.207 --> 00:11:23.308
I&nbsp;just came from shopping!

00:11:23.308 --> 00:11:24.289
Do you want a lift?

00:11:24.289 --> 00:11:26.093
- Yeah, can we pop in here?

00:11:26.093 --> 00:11:27.720
Of course, but we have to find some room!

00:11:35.205 --> 00:11:35.985
Let's go!

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:38.408
- That's nice here with the air conditioning&nbsp;on!

00:11:38.408 --> 00:11:40.793
Yes, it's very refreshing!

00:11:41.559 --> 00:11:43.246
- I can see that!

00:11:44.520 --> 00:11:46.179
Do you like driving in the pickup?

00:11:46.179 --> 00:11:46.679
- A lot, yeah!

00:11:46.679 --> 00:11:49.259
It's like a couch!

00:11:49.259 --> 00:11:54.738
Not necessarily in this weather,
 but yeah, in general, it's&nbsp;cool.

00:11:56.742 --> 00:11:58.137
- You went to get some food?

00:11:58.137 --> 00:12:05.940
Yeah, I went to Nuno's and the Bulk Store,
 and I got&nbsp;some supplies, some veggies, some old stuff...

00:12:07.500 --> 00:12:08.816
- It's your weekly routine?

00:12:08.816 --> 00:12:12.505
My weekly routine exactly.

00:12:12.505 --> 00:12:13.542
- All right! Thanks!

00:12:13.542 --> 00:12:16.660
Would you mind helping me 
carrying some stuff to the storage container?

00:12:16.660 --> 00:12:17.396
- Sure!

00:12:17.396 --> 00:12:18.546
Which one? This guy?

00:12:19.371 --> 00:12:20.985
- That, and maybe some more over there?

00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:26.160
All right! Thanks for the ride!

00:12:29.280 --> 00:12:32.135
So, here we have the storage container.

00:12:33.284 --> 00:12:36.300
It's where we drop all our dried food.

00:12:37.140 --> 00:12:38.018
Hey Alan!

00:12:38.195 --> 00:12:39.232
- How's it going?

00:12:41.415 --> 00:12:43.665
I can show you the container.

00:12:45.960 --> 00:12:48.525
I'll just give it to you here, Timo.

00:12:48.525 --> 00:12:49.220
- Thank&nbsp;you.

00:12:49.220 --> 00:12:51.412
Then, we can continue the tour.

00:12:51.412 --> 00:12:52.922
But, it's great having this!

00:12:52.922 --> 00:12:55.052
- Have a nice tour.

00:12:55.052 --> 00:12:56.056
Thanks!

00:12:56.056 --> 00:12:59.218
So, here's&nbsp;the more sort of landscaping area in the container.

00:12:59.218 --> 00:13:05.437
With all the tools chainsaws and brush cutters that we work with.

00:13:06.910 --> 00:13:07.852
What are you doing?

00:13:07.852 --> 00:13:12.710
- Well, General Help has been hard at work,
 and all of our tools need sharpening.

00:13:12.710 --> 00:13:14.143
So, I've been working on that...

00:13:14.939 --> 00:13:16.283
- Are you good with sharpening?

00:13:16.283 --> 00:13:19.089
Yeah! I think you can see that the tools&nbsp;are quite sharp...

00:13:19.089 --> 00:13:22.169
I don't know if I'd say the same about myself, but...

00:13:22.169 --> 00:13:25.054
- Okay, but your fingers are still&nbsp;on,
 so maybe it means they're not sharp enough...

00:13:25.054 --> 00:13:26.147
Exactly, exactly.

00:13:26.147 --> 00:13:28.238
There could be uh some more work in here

00:13:28.238 --> 00:13:30.251
Cool! All right.

00:13:31.223 --> 00:13:33.595
Well, good luck with that!

00:13:37.631 --> 00:13:39.719
Adrian I think used to be&nbsp;here as well?

00:13:39.719 --> 00:13:40.584
Hey Adrian!

00:13:40.584 --> 00:13:41.452
- What's up Dave?

00:13:41.452 --> 00:13:42.653
Good, you?

00:13:42.653 --> 00:13:45.476
- Good! I'm working on by digester, but...

00:13:45.476 --> 00:13:46.315
Go away, go away!

00:13:46.315 --> 00:13:47.397
No spoilers, no&nbsp;spoilers!

00:13:47.397 --> 00:13:48.347
That's for later!

00:13:48.347 --> 00:13:51.254
- That's for later, when we're setting up a biogas system.

00:13:51.254 --> 00:13:53.340
For later...

00:13:54.489 --> 00:13:56.426
Okay, let's see more stuff!

00:13:56.426 --> 00:13:58.666
Now,&nbsp;we have the workspace to go to.

00:13:58.666 --> 00:13:59.930
We're currently back in Basekamp!

00:13:59.930 --> 00:14:01.805
This is where we started originally.

00:14:02.188 --> 00:14:06.668
Here we have Jaime, who is doing some stuff.

00:14:06.668 --> 00:14:08.202
I don't know...

00:14:08.526 --> 00:14:09.871
Let's see what he's doing.

00:14:10.608 --> 00:14:11.715
Hey Jaime!

00:14:11.715 --> 00:14:12.316
- Hello!

00:14:12.316 --> 00:14:15.378
I'm trying&nbsp;to find drill bits.

00:14:15.378 --> 00:14:20.070
One specific drill bit, like everything is a bit a mess around here...

00:14:20.070 --> 00:14:21.021
- How come?

00:14:21.021 --> 00:14:26.284
A lot of people are using the tools,
 and all the stuff we have in here.

00:14:26.284 --> 00:14:29.438
Not everybody comes back with it,
 or&nbsp;everything comes back at the same time.

00:14:29.438 --> 00:14:31.465
So, yeah, I'm looking...

00:14:31.465 --> 00:14:32.825
- A community workspace, huh?

00:14:32.825 --> 00:14:34.014
A community workspace, yeah...

00:14:34.014 --> 00:14:36.407
- Cool, and&nbsp;how is it in the heat in this black box?

00:14:36.407 --> 00:14:39.889
I mean, I'm not spending a lot of time in here, but it's hot!

00:14:39.889 --> 00:14:41.113
It's really hot!

00:14:41.113 --> 00:14:44.277
Just come here for tools, and get out of here.

00:14:44.277 --> 00:14:46.682
- Yeah, it's basically a&nbsp;big toolbox now.

00:14:46.682 --> 00:14:48.180
A big metal box.

00:14:48.840 --> 00:14:49.632
- Cool! All right!

00:14:49.632 --> 00:14:51.626
And the rest of the guys are in&nbsp;the pig trailer?

00:14:51.626 --> 00:14:53.031
- Yep, downstairs.

00:14:53.031 --> 00:14:56.661
Cool, then, well, let's have a look at that!

00:14:56.661 --> 00:14:58.252
Good luck finding&nbsp;your tool!

00:14:58.252 --> 00:14:59.737
Sounds fun...

00:15:00.798 --> 00:15:07.399
So, now, we can go to the pig trailer,
 which we recently bought thanks&nbsp;to our Patreons!

00:15:07.399 --> 00:15:10.073
It's down here.

00:15:10.073 --> 00:15:14.539
It's not a very official path here...

00:15:14.539 --> 00:15:17.259
This is next to&nbsp;our well, where we get our water.

00:15:17.259 --> 00:15:20.141
We recently did a small update actually!

00:15:20.141 --> 00:15:23.460
We installed the sensor&nbsp;that can measure
 the height of the water level.

00:15:24.960 --> 00:15:29.677
It's to see, especially in these hot days,&nbsp;
if the water level goes down or up.

00:15:29.677 --> 00:15:32.589
So, we can keep track of it, to make sure it's not empty.

00:15:32.589 --> 00:15:34.320
But,&nbsp;you can see more of that in the research module!

00:15:35.400 --> 00:15:37.533
So, let's continue here on this path.

00:15:37.533 --> 00:15:39.099
A small update also...

00:15:39.099 --> 00:15:40.500
A kind of a big one!

00:15:41.520 --> 00:15:44.783
Just this week, we finally bought this middle&nbsp;piece of land!

00:15:44.783 --> 00:15:48.494
It was originally not ours,
 and we made a video about that a few weeks ago.

00:15:48.494 --> 00:15:49.980
It had a lot of views actually, which is cool.

00:15:51.360 --> 00:15:53.673
It was kind of weird that the middle land was not from us...

00:15:53.673 --> 00:15:56.784
But now, we've been talking with the neighbor,
 and now we finally bought it!

00:15:56.784 --> 00:16:00.540
Now,&nbsp;we are on our land, and not on the neighbors land anymore!

00:16:02.280 --> 00:16:06.105
So, the pig trailer is around here.

00:16:06.105 --> 00:16:10.083
You&nbsp;have to go through this little maze...

00:16:10.083 --> 00:16:13.826
We made this pathway to also get electricity, 
because we&nbsp;don't have any there...

00:16:15.287 --> 00:16:18.679
But, we needed to work on the pig trailer,
and to be able to use the tools we have,

00:16:21.567 --> 00:16:22.860
We kind of need electricity...

00:16:24.780 --> 00:16:33.120
This was chopped not too long ago,
 but stuff&nbsp;always grows back here very fast!

00:16:34.935 --> 00:16:36.502
As you can see here, there are a lot of brambles

00:16:37.769 --> 00:16:40.440
There she is: the pig trailer!

00:16:40.440 --> 00:16:42.651
We have to go down here on this wall.

00:16:42.651 --> 00:16:44.483
We don't really have a proper&nbsp;stairs yet...

00:16:44.483 --> 00:16:48.090
So, I hope that's gonna be okay.

00:16:48.915 --> 00:16:52.254
It's maybe also a good moment, 
where you can guys see a sweaty&nbsp;video maker!

00:16:52.784 --> 00:16:54.360
This is Javi right here!

00:16:54.360 --> 00:16:55.910
- Moving on!

00:16:58.119 --> 00:16:59.169
Thank you, Dave.

00:16:59.169 --> 00:17:00.389
- Alright-y!

00:17:00.389 --> 00:17:00.889
All is okay!

00:17:01.332 --> 00:17:02.199
- All right!

00:17:02.759 --> 00:17:04.897
So, the pig trailer.

00:17:05.604 --> 00:17:10.518
We're hard at work trying to convert this 
into a little house to live in.

00:17:11.314 --> 00:17:15.699
We have set up a little&nbsp;workstation here, where we can work.

00:17:15.699 --> 00:17:19.430
It's just so we don't have to walk to 
the workspace each time&nbsp;with some tools...

00:17:19.872 --> 00:17:21.058
How's it going here?

00:17:22.414 --> 00:17:24.019
- It's going all right!

00:17:24.019 --> 00:17:25.080
Whatcha making?

00:17:25.080 --> 00:17:27.241
- I'm making a nice frame for the door.

00:17:27.241 --> 00:17:31.247
I got some old door posts here.

00:17:33.516 --> 00:17:37.520
I'm gonna&nbsp;make a nice frame, and then we put it in here!

00:17:38.640 --> 00:17:41.156
Then, the door is open for you to enter the house.

00:17:41.156 --> 00:17:42.679
- Cool! Can&nbsp;we have a look inside?

00:17:42.679 --> 00:17:43.833
Yes!

00:17:44.363 --> 00:17:45.329
Watch your steps!

00:17:46.802 --> 00:17:49.583
- I will...

00:17:50.280 --> 00:17:53.625
So, yeah, here's a preview of the house.

00:17:53.625 --> 00:17:55.520
There's&nbsp;going to be living room and a bedroom.

00:17:55.520 --> 00:18:00.460
It still requires imagination,
 but maybe we will also put a roof on&nbsp;top.

00:18:00.460 --> 00:18:01.802
Probably...

00:18:01.802 --> 00:18:04.730
Isn't it hard to work in the heat here?

00:18:05.290 --> 00:18:06.805
- It's okay with some shade!

00:18:06.805 --> 00:18:12.035
A really nice tarp with a cool breeze with a t-shirt contest.

00:18:12.978 --> 00:18:15.749
- All right! You don't seem to struggle with it!

00:18:15.749 --> 00:18:17.618
Cool! Well, good&nbsp;luck!

00:18:17.618 --> 00:18:19.709
Here we have Robert!

00:18:19.709 --> 00:18:22.824
He's from Iceland and he's always wearing a lot of clothes!

00:18:22.824 --> 00:18:24.298
I don't know how he does that.

00:18:24.298 --> 00:18:25.819
What's your secret?

00:18:26.400 --> 00:18:27.526
- Don't think about it.

00:18:28.086 --> 00:18:29.123
''Don't think about it.''

00:18:29.123 --> 00:18:31.501
Cool!&nbsp;I'll keep that in mind for next time.

00:18:32.768 --> 00:18:34.034
Good luck!

00:18:36.300 --> 00:18:41.331
So, now, we need to go kind of far away on the land.

00:18:42.981 --> 00:18:46.878
We also build a few things there,
 because most of the time we spend here.

00:18:46.878 --> 00:18:48.959
It's quite central and it's all&nbsp;in one place.

00:18:48.959 --> 00:18:51.855
We're trying to keep all the infrastructure 
together and the people together.

00:18:51.855 --> 00:18:55.080
So, it's a bit&nbsp;easier to manage, but also for fire.

00:18:56.820 --> 00:18:59.600
Now, we're going to go to more the lower part of the land

00:18:59.600 --> 00:19:02.769
It's a bit further away with a bit of different 
vegetation as well, which is cool!

00:19:03.506 --> 00:19:06.536
But, it's gonna be quite a walk...

00:19:06.536 --> 00:19:09.689
We're currently walking on a new road we made!

00:19:09.689 --> 00:19:11.724
Maybe you can see it when I walk here?

00:19:11.724 --> 00:19:17.160
It's a big rough road straight through the mimosas,
but it&nbsp;was needed to deliver the pig trailer to the land.

00:19:18.180 --> 00:19:22.315
Well, yeah, we still need to make this
 more nicer and proper a bit...

00:19:23.140 --> 00:19:25.146
But, yeah, we will make it good.

00:19:25.794 --> 00:19:29.605
Now, I'm just trying to fill up the&nbsp;time
 basically before we get there...

00:19:29.605 --> 00:19:33.451
So, I thought maybe I can tell you a joke,
 but I don't really have one...

00:19:33.451 --> 00:19:35.211
maybe you have a joke!

00:19:35.211 --> 00:19:36.928
leave jokes in the comments if you have one I can use&nbsp;
it next time

00:19:36.928 --> 00:19:40.800
but instead of me talking

00:19:46.213 --> 00:19:47.843
Can we can speed it up?

00:19:49.248 --> 00:19:54.390
You don't have to listen to this, and you can just sit back.

00:19:54.714 --> 00:19:59.176
We'll walk to the lower part of the land,
 and&nbsp;we'll meet you there again!

00:19:59.728 --> 00:20:02.142
So, let's speed it up!

00:20:19.734 --> 00:20:23.137
All right, so, here we are at the bottom of the&nbsp;land.

00:20:23.844 --> 00:20:27.133
There used to be a pathway here, but we don't come here often!

00:20:27.133 --> 00:20:31.020
So, as you can see,&nbsp;it gets a bit adventurous to go through here.

00:20:31.800 --> 00:20:34.912
Every time, we have to go a little&nbsp;bit lower.

00:20:34.912 --> 00:20:35.820
It keeps us flexible!

00:20:37.440 --> 00:20:40.906
But, this is the part where we found 
an old&nbsp;well from the neighbors.

00:20:41.702 --> 00:20:43.293
It's right here!

00:20:44.324 --> 00:20:45.789
It's quite impressive.

00:20:45.789 --> 00:20:50.207
In the winter time,&nbsp;it was really almost until the edge full of water.

00:20:50.207 --> 00:20:51.363
Now, it's very low...

00:20:51.363 --> 00:20:54.960
I can throw in something&nbsp;just for you guys,
 so you can see how deep it is.

00:20:58.385 --> 00:21:00.476
It was only a little bit of water right&nbsp;now.

00:21:00.476 --> 00:21:02.936
But, yeah, it's also hot and the middle of the summer...

00:21:02.936 --> 00:21:05.743
It's nice to keep an eye on the water levels like this one.

00:21:05.743 --> 00:21:07.980
Let's continue here.

00:21:10.080 --> 00:21:13.933
This is where we have our big grass field!

00:21:14.434 --> 00:21:17.901
A big patch&nbsp;the bottom of the land, and close to the creek.

00:21:19.440 --> 00:21:22.992
This is where we potentially have a Project Kamp festival one day!

00:21:23.611 --> 00:21:24.947
Unless you have other ideas!

00:21:24.947 --> 00:21:28.159
We're still looking for good ideas&nbsp;
on what to do with this big piece of land.

00:21:29.384 --> 00:21:31.094
But, we're gonna go right there!

00:21:31.594 --> 00:21:36.374
Which is a&nbsp;bit of a place of land we created
 where we can relax a bit more.

00:21:36.374 --> 00:21:43.055
Just so we aren't always&nbsp;in the middle of Basekamp,
 where all the people are and all the noises from the workspace...

00:21:43.055 --> 00:21:44.713
So, here, it's much more calm.

00:21:44.713 --> 00:21:46.260
It's always a few degrees colder.

00:21:47.100 --> 00:21:51.573
Yeah, it's quite a nice place to relax a bit more.

00:21:52.899 --> 00:21:59.477
This also has our, I would say, biggest tree on the land?

00:21:59.477 --> 00:22:01.217
I&nbsp;guess it also has the oldest tree

00:22:01.217 --> 00:22:02.340
It's an old cork tree.

00:22:03.060 --> 00:22:07.592
Most of it burned down, except for&nbsp;this guy,
 because it has a thick bark.

00:22:07.592 --> 00:22:11.765
So, it's a bit more fire resilient, 
and we put a yoga deck&nbsp;underneath.

00:22:11.765 --> 00:22:15.420
It's a nice place to relax at.

00:22:16.860 --> 00:22:19.974
Over here, we have a little tent that&nbsp;we built.

00:22:19.974 --> 00:22:22.124
You might have seen it a few updates ago.

00:22:22.124 --> 00:22:26.926
The goal was to try to make a tent
 for staying here for a longer period of time.

00:22:26.926 --> 00:22:31.055
It's a bit more of a comfortable tent,
so you can also&nbsp;stand in there.

00:22:31.055 --> 00:22:32.280
It's not always bending forward...

00:22:32.880 --> 00:22:34.822
It feels a bit more like a little house!

00:22:34.822 --> 00:22:39.840
So, yeah, this is what it looks like now.

00:22:43.860 --> 00:22:48.850
There's no one really permanently in here,&nbsp;
but it's used for guests or every now and&nbsp;some people

00:22:49.204 --> 00:22:53.011
Because, we're also still gathering&nbsp;feedback and it's really a prototype.

00:22:53.011 --> 00:22:54.529
We're trying to improve it!

00:22:54.529 --> 00:23:01.741
A few things: the canvas is a bit tight, 
the decking on the floor has a few gaps, so insects get in...

00:23:01.741 --> 00:23:04.042
So, yeah, it's version one!

00:23:04.042 --> 00:23:09.976
We're now considering if we build a new version,
like a completely new tent,&nbsp;or maybe we change this one.

00:23:09.976 --> 00:23:11.100
We're not sure yet...

00:23:12.360 --> 00:23:18.465
But, now, what we're actually gonna do is the final part!

00:23:18.995 --> 00:23:20.694
Which I like a lot!

00:23:20.694 --> 00:23:23.104
Maybe the best part.

00:23:25.078 --> 00:23:27.198
You've seen it before, if&nbsp;you follow these videos!

00:23:27.198 --> 00:23:33.561
It's our waterfall, it's our lagoon, 
and it's the place which we've cleaned up&nbsp;a lot before.

00:23:33.561 --> 00:23:36.900
We can cool down, relax, and take a swim!

00:23:37.740 --> 00:23:43.020
Which is particularly nice in these&nbsp;very hot days
 to get some refreshment!

00:23:45.180 --> 00:23:47.448
So, we go right here!

00:23:48.332 --> 00:23:53.365
This is also the&nbsp;place where most 
of the people go at the end of the day.

00:23:53.365 --> 00:23:55.586
Or, even lunch time, or&nbsp;in the mornings.

00:23:56.087 --> 00:23:58.881
They go in chill and take a dip.

00:23:59.280 --> 00:24:01.843
So, it's been very good to have it on the land.

00:24:01.843 --> 00:24:06.128
We're now also entering the neighbors land,
 so it's actually not on our land...

00:24:06.128 --> 00:24:11.100
But, the neighbor has&nbsp;been very kind to offer this,
 so that we can use it.

00:24:12.300 --> 00:24:13.758
It's really nice here as well!

00:24:13.758 --> 00:24:19.032
It has much more&nbsp;native trees growing,
because it has much more water in this part of the land.

00:24:19.032 --> 00:24:22.551
It still has mimosas as&nbsp;well, but yeah...

00:24:23.111 --> 00:24:25.622
So, we're almost there!

00:24:26.683 --> 00:24:28.039
Right here!

00:24:30.360 --> 00:24:33.720
It's also funny, because when we came&nbsp;here,
there was no pathway here.

00:24:33.720 --> 00:24:38.042
But, the more people just go to certain places, pathways show up.

00:24:38.042 --> 00:24:44.100
It's a bit like when you have snow, 
and you&nbsp;suddenly see all the traces where people have walked.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:44.760 --> 00:24:48.720
You can see what is actually the most&nbsp;used pathways
from cars or people walking.

00:24:49.500 --> 00:24:50.956
So, we have that here as well.

00:24:50.956 --> 00:24:53.511
Slowly, the pathways&nbsp;rise up.

00:24:55.104 --> 00:24:56.891
Yeah, I like that!

00:24:56.891 --> 00:25:01.889
But, as you can notice, I'm also just killing some time 
to make sure we enter&nbsp;the lagoon.

00:25:02.832 --> 00:25:05.443
You guys can see it over there!

00:25:06.720 --> 00:25:09.251
Here, we also have a lot of big old rocks!

00:25:09.251 --> 00:25:10.963
It's cool.

00:25:10.963 --> 00:25:12.194
No one knows how old is this!

00:25:12.194 --> 00:25:16.155
They just say it's very old,
 but I would love to know how&nbsp;old it is.

00:25:16.921 --> 00:25:20.026
So, if anyone can tell us, let us know!

00:25:21.900 --> 00:25:22.990
Here we are!

00:25:26.786 --> 00:25:29.311
It's a bit&nbsp;overgrown currently.

00:25:29.311 --> 00:25:30.534
We need to maintain it...

00:25:31.123 --> 00:25:32.816
But, it grows fast as well!

00:25:32.816 --> 00:25:34.633
Everything is wet, and there is a lot of sun.

00:25:37.175 --> 00:25:38.846
You can keep on doing this!

00:25:38.846 --> 00:25:40.575
We'll do more towards the end of the summer.

00:25:40.575 --> 00:25:43.495
As you&nbsp;can see, the water is also quite low.

00:25:43.495 --> 00:25:46.247
So, it is not really 'waterfall', but more of a 'waterdrip'.

00:25:46.807 --> 00:25:47.856
But, it's still nice!

00:25:48.976 --> 00:25:50.714
And then, we go up here...

00:25:54.960 --> 00:25:55.920
Hey Otis!

00:25:59.100 --> 00:26:00.895
So, we used to hang out more in the bottom part.

00:26:00.895 --> 00:26:05.389
But then, this year, we cleaned up the top part,
 where there is a lagoon.

00:26:05.389 --> 00:26:10.440
So, this is now where you can take a nice dip and cool down.

00:26:11.760 --> 00:26:14.423
The water level used to be until the yellow door.

00:26:14.423 --> 00:26:15.900
I'm not sure if you can see that...

00:26:15.900 --> 00:26:20.940
So, it's already quite low, 
but there's still water inside to&nbsp;cool down.

00:26:20.940 --> 00:26:23.797
But, we're not sure if it will be there all summer...

00:26:23.797 --> 00:26:27.120
It's the first time we have a&nbsp;lagoon, so we're still figuring it out.

00:26:33.212 --> 00:26:35.040
Over here, we can relax.

00:26:37.500 --> 00:26:40.281
That was kind of it for this&nbsp;video!

00:26:41.018 --> 00:26:46.636
In the next video, we're gonna show you 
how to make a roof from cans!

00:26:47.284 --> 00:26:48.742
Kevin can do that.

00:26:48.742 --> 00:26:49.999
- Yes, with these things!

00:26:53.472 --> 00:26:56.199
If you already want to see that video,
 make sure to support us on Patreon!

00:26:56.199 --> 00:26:59.588
You can see the video one week ahead in 4K.

00:26:59.588 --> 00:27:02.760
If not, we'll just see you next week here on YouTube!

00:27:05.483 --> 00:27:07.591
Okay, that was a long, long walk...

00:27:07.591 --> 00:27:08.789
All right! Thanks!

00:27:08.789 --> 00:27:10.620
We're gonna take swim now, and we'll see you next video!

00:27:15.021 --> 00:27:15.898
Yuuuuup!

00:27:15.898 --> 00:27:17.271
- He got it!

